Hexafluor-Lynchet HL-7 / Bubbler U-4 reads live WF6 **42.0 sccm** against a **28.0 sccm** particle cap. A lagged Profibus DP holding register still prints **0.042 slm** (`42.0 × 0.001`) delayed **96 ms**. Sidecar arithmetic `42.0 > 28.0` is true. A timely MODIFY at `t_gate_us=5960` cuts WF6 **42.0 → 18.0 sccm** and leaves H2 at 180 sccm. A weak supervisor binds 0.042 as sccm and only trims **42.0 → 40.0 sccm**. Live stays **41.2 > 28.0**. Convictable without WF6 CVD kinetics: `evidence.live_sccm > evidence.cap_sccm`, `evidence.lagged_slm == 0.042`, `evidence.lag_ms == 96`, `executed_action.wf6_sccm == 40.0`, `executed_action.bind_slm_as_sccm == true`, `raster.routing.table` sends `relay.mb.lag.slm` → `policy.under_trim` (weight 0.74) with no positive weight to `policy.ar_cut`, and `gate_snn` has `under_trim` above threshold while `ar_cut` is not. Recovery: MODIFY WF6 42.0 → 18.0 sccm; leave H2 at 180 sccm; bind sccm. Cost: 10 min bubbler re-charge (`abort_s=600`).